WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.105
This lesson is designed to be interactive For each
idea first read the explanation

00:00:06.132 --> 00:00:11.053
and look at the example Before you run the code make
a quick prediction about

00:00:11.079 --> 00:00:16.648
what Python will produce Next run the example in the
browser

00:00:17.585 --> 00:00:21.374
After you see the output change one small part of
the code such as a

00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:27.164
number or a text value and run it again Finally
explain to yourself what changed

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:32.963
and why The code editor is styled like VS Code so
the environment feels

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:38.426
familiar when you later work in a local editor For
larger assignments you may also

00:00:38.452 --> 00:00:44.149
use Jupyter Notebook JupyterLab Colab or another
Python environment The

00:00:44.163 --> 00:00:49.939
important part is not the tool The important part is
understanding the relationship between

00:00:49.965 --> 00:00:52.228
the code the data and the result
